{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "The Environment", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Our Environment", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe environmental change in social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Present Continuous Tense: Passive and Active Forms", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> in both active and passive structures. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Active</span>: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">People</span> (subject) <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">are pouring</span> toxic waste </span>(object) <span class=\"italic\">into our lakes and rivers, ruining the clean water.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Passive</span>:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Toxic waste </span>(subject)<span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">is being poured</span> into our lakes and rivers, ruining the clean water </span>(by people).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in academic and scientific writing. In the example above, <span class=\"italic\">people</span> is the agent.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below to see the form of the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span>  passive:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">is/was/were</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">being</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">past participle</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Toxic waste</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">is</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">being</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">poured</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The amount of garbage that</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">is</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">being</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">created</span>.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "But what is humankind doing to the environment?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Toxic waste is being poured into our lakes and rivers, ruining the clean water.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "As the population grows, it has become almost impossible to deal with the amount of garbage that is being created. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Although wildlife preservation groups try to clean the birds, only some of them are making it back to the sea alive.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Present Perfect Tense: Active and Passive Forms", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Present Perfect passive to talk about the same kind of actions or events.  <br/>The passive shifts the focus from the doer of the action (<span class=\"italic\">agent</span>) to the receiver of the action. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">Our air <span class=\"strong\">has been made</span> unfit to breathe in many big cities by cars, trucks, and factory emissions. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In this example, the agent is cars, trucks and factory emissions. In a passive clause, you usually use <span class=\"italic\">by</span> to introduce the agent. Agents are not used often in passive clauses. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below to see the form of the Present Perfect passive:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Subject</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">has/have</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">been</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Our air</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">has</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">been</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">made</span> ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Elephants and whales</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">have </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">been</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">put</span> ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Our air has been made unfit to breathe in many big cities by cars, trucks, and factory emissions. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "As the population grows, it has become almost impossible to deal with the amount of garbage that is being created. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Oil spills have caused thousands of ducks and other animals to die from contamination in the water.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Hunting has also put many species of animals in danger. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Animals like the panda, the whale, and the elephant have all been put at risk of becoming extinct. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "unfit ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not good enough to do or to be used", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Our air has been made unfit to breathe.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about the environmental problems.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "factory ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a building where goods are produced in large quantities, by machines", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Our air has been made unfit to breathe because of cars, trucks, and factory emissions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "emissions ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a gas or other substance sent into the air", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Factory emissions cause problems in air quality.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "toxic waste", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a harmful substance which causes health problems and negatively affects the environment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Toxic waste is being poured into our lakes and rivers, ruining the clean water.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "pile ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a heap; a mass", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Piles of garbage now litter some of the most beautiful nature sites.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to litter", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to throw garbage or waste on the ground", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Piles of garbage litter some of the most beautiful nature sites.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "oil spill", "type": "name"}, {"content": "crude oil released into a body of water", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Oil spills have caused thousands of ducks and other animals to die.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "contamination", "type": "name"}, {"content": "pollution by a poisonous or hazardous substance", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Thousands of ducks and other animals die from contamination in the water.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "hunting ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "chasing and killing animals for food or sport", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Hunting has also put many species of animals in danger.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob01aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "awareness ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "perception; understanding", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We can only hope that awareness can help us limit the damage we do.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob01aud10", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Ask 4 or 5 friends the following questions:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What do you consider is the most serious environmental issue? Why?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What do you do to help the planet?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Don't forget to take notes of their answers. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepare a written summary of the answers. Use the passive in your writing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your summary with other classmates.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I take a survey about environmental issues.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a summary of the survey results.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my summary with others.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"content": "engenn9le02ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "video", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "Our environment is everything around us. It's the air we breathe, the water we drink, and the earth we leave for future generations. But what is humankind doing to the environment?\nOne of the biggest problems today is pollution. Our air has been made unfit to breathe in many big cities by cars, trucks, and factory emissions. But that's not all. Toxic waste is being poured into our lakes and rivers, ruining the clean water."}, {"image": "", "time": "31000", "id": 2, "text": "Garbage is another serious environmental problem. As the population grows, it has become almost impossible to deal with the amount of garbage that is being created. Piles of garbage now litter some of the most beautiful nature sites.\nHuman actions do not only affect human lives, they also impact the lives of wildlife. Oil spills have caused thousands of ducks and other animals to die from contamination in the water.\nAlthough wildlife preservation groups try to clean the birds, only some of them are making it back to the sea alive."}, {"image": "", "time": "67000", "id": 3, "text": "Hunting has also put many species of animals in danger. Animals like the panda, the whale, and the elephant have all been put at risk of becoming extinct. Laws against hunting can save these animals.\nIt is not too late to save our environment. We can only hope that awareness can help us limit the damage we do. We'll then be able to leave a cleaner and healthier environment to future generations."}], "video_src": "engenn9le02ob01re2vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can describe environmental problems.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things that are happening. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things that have happened. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you consider yourself to be environmentally aware? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " In your opinion, what are some of the world's biggest environmental problems?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Is it too late to save our environment?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " How are <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">wildlife preservation groups</span> trying to help?", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"content": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">\"Wildlife preservation groups\"</span> are groups that try to help and protec